WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:10.740
A calling platform sees every call it places. It cannot see the ones staff placed by hand through the CRM's own dialer, and those are the calls a lead remembers.

2
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:23.500
A scheduled scan asks the vendor for calls this system never placed, skips any it has examined, and decides whether each connected: the vendor's status, and twenty seconds.

3
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:35.460
The page before the scan has ever run, on a keyless local copy of the platform, with invented rows. It is off by default, because examining a call spends credit.

4
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:49.100
Where the vendor has a transcript, the job takes it. Where it does not, it transcribes the recording. 5,147 of 6,260 came from the fallback.

5
00:00:50.200 --> 00:01:03.660
Sales or support is decided by four deterministic signals before a model is asked. The first of them, the vendor's tags, decided 6,109 of 6,257.

6
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:20.730
Three near-duplicate vendor columns were kept on every row, to settle from data which one was authoritative. 0 of 8,820 carry a value in any of them. On a keyless local copy, with invented rows.

7
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:33.240
Read from the platform's own tables on 28 September 2026, each figure with the number it is out of. No transcript, summary or flag text is quoted.

8
00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:45.400
Every examined call lands in exactly one of four branches, so a missing score is explained by the row. On a keyless local copy of the platform, with invented rows.

9
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:58.520
The model writes a flag; nothing records anyone opening the row. The five dimensions behind each score are stored and never rendered. The rows with no score make the rest trustworthy.
